        fp: "Defendant and an accomplice agreed to break into an unoccupied home at night to steal electronic equipment. Defendant acted as the lookout on the street, while the acquaintance forced open a rear window and entered the home. While the acquaintance was inside gathering laptops, an armed private neighborhood security patrol officer walked up the driveway, spotted the broken window, and drew his service firearm. The acquaintance stepped out of the back door carrying a backpack. The security officer shouted, 'Security, freeze!' The acquaintance immediately pulled a semi-automatic handgun from his waistband and fired three shots at the officer, wounding the officer in the chest. Defendant, who had remained on the sidewalk, heard the gunshots, panicked, and fled on foot before being arrested two blocks away. Defendant was unarmed and had no prior knowledge that the acquaintance was carrying a firearm. The jurisdiction adheres to traditional common law principles of conspiracy and accomplice liability.",
