        fp: "Defendant and an acquaintance agreed to rob an armored cash delivery courier during a scheduled bank pickup. Defendant's role was to act as the armed gunman who would disarm the courier, while the acquaintance drove the getaway car. On the morning of the planned robbery, Defendant woke up with severe moral remorse, threw his handgun into a river, and decided to abandon the enterprise. Two hours before the scheduled heist, Defendant called the acquaintance and stated: 'I am not going to do this. I threw away my gun, I am quitting, and you should call it off too.' The acquaintance replied, 'You're a coward, but I don't need you; I'll rob the courier myself.' Defendant hung up and stayed home. The acquaintance recruited an independent third party, drove to the bank, held up the courier with a shotgun, stole $200,000, and escaped. The jurisdiction adheres to traditional common law rules of conspiracy and accomplice liability.",
